sentences.i:
Whoever says love begins by choice, * tell him, “You lie: it is compulsion, all of it;
and where there is compulsion there is no shame.” * Reports bear witness that this is true,
never forged against the sound …

sentences.l:
And if you wish, then say: a torment that is sweet, * or a throbbing in the entrails, or a blow,
or a blessing, or a vengeance, or a craving * by which the soul takes comfort, or perishes;
it has run between its reverse and the straight.

sentences.i:
Call it, if you will, a torment that is sweet, * a throbbing in the heart, a blow;
a blessing or a punishment, a craving * the soul delights in or is ruined by:
it runs both ways, straight and reversed.

sentences.l:
And with this, its days are festivals, * and their mouth is on the continuance smiling,
and the breaths of their perfume are festivals, * and it, for everything that disgraces, is a cutter-off;
it has never lodged-in the heart of a base, vile one.
